---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import SearchOverlay from '../../components/SearchOverlay.astro';
import BlogRating from '../../components/BlogRating.astro';
import BlogShare from '../../components/BlogShare.astro';

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BlogPosting",
  "headline": "Top 5 Free Online PDF Tools for Editing, Merging, and Protecting Documents",
  "description": "Discover the top 5 free online PDF tools that allow you to merge, split, flatten, and protect your PDF documents securely in your browser.",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "SolversPro"
  },
  "datePublished": new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Top 5 Free Online PDF Tools | SolversPro Blog"
  description="Discover the best free online PDF tools to merge, split, flatten, and protect your PDF documents securely and directly in your browser."
  schema={schema}
>
  <Header />
  <SearchOverlay />

  <main class="flex-1 py-16 px-6">
    <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Header -->
      <header class="mb-12">
        <nav aria-label="breadcrumb" class="mb-6">
          <ol class="flex items-center space-x-2 text-sm text-zinc-400">
            <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Home</a></li>
            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
              <a href="/blog" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Blog</a>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"></path></svg>
              <span class="text-[#ff6b35]">Guides</span>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </nav>
        
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-6 leading-tight">Top 5 Free Online PDF Tools for Editing, Merging, and Protecting Documents</h1>
        
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-zinc-400 mb-8 pb-8 border-b border-white/[0.06]">
          <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 7V3m8 4V3m-9 8h10M5 21h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z"></path></svg>
            July 20, 2026
          </span>
          <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>
            5 min read
          </span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Content -->
      <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:text-white prose-a:text-[#2dd4bf] hover:prose-a:text-[#5eead4] prose-strong:text-white">
        <p class="lead text-xl text-zinc-300 mb-8">
          Working with PDF files doesn't have to be a frustrating experience involving expensive desktop software or shady websites that store your sensitive documents. At SolversPro, we believe in providing secure, fast, and free online PDF tools that run entirely in your browser.
        </p>

        <p>
          Whether you're compiling a report, splitting a massive ebook, or trying to secure confidential information, here are the top 5 free online PDF tools you should add to your daily workflow.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">1. The PDF Merger: Combine Documents Seamlessly</h2>
        <p>
          Combining multiple documents into a single file is one of the most common PDF tasks. Our <a href="/tools/pdf-merger">PDF Merger Tool</a> allows you to drag and drop multiple PDF files, arrange them in the exact order you need, and combine them into a single, cohesive document.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because the merging happens 100% locally in your browser, your files are never uploaded to our servers, ensuring your sensitive data remains completely private.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">2. Split PDFs by Range or Pages</h2>
        <p>
          Sometimes you only need a few pages out of a massive 500-page manual. We offer two specialized tools for this:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong><a href="/tools/pdf-split-pages">Extract Specific Pages:</a></strong> Perfect when you need non-consecutive pages (e.g., pages 1, 5, and 12).</li>
          <li><strong><a href="/tools/pdf-split-range">Split by Page Range:</a></strong> Ideal for extracting a contiguous chapter or section (e.g., pages 10-25).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">3. Protect and Encrypt Your PDFs</h2>
        <p>
          Sharing sensitive financial records, contracts, or personal documents? You should always password-protect them first. The <a href="/tools/pdf-protect">PDF Password Protector</a> encrypts your document using industry-standard security. You can set a strong password so only authorized recipients can open the file.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">4. Flatten PDFs for Read-Only Sharing</h2>
        <p>
          If you have a fillable PDF form and you want to lock the fields so the recipient can't change the data you entered, you need to flatten the document. The <a href="/tools/pdf-flatten">PDF Flatten Tool</a> bakes your text inputs directly into the document's visual layer, making it read-only and ensuring it prints exactly as it appears on screen.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">5. Convert Images to PDF</h2>
        <p>
          Need to compile a batch of receipts, photos, or scanned documents into a single presentation? The <a href="/tools/images-to-pdf">Images to PDF Converter</a> supports JPG, PNG, and WebP formats. Just drag them in, rearrange the order, and generate a clean PDF document instantly.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/[0.06] rounded-xl p-8 my-12">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4 mt-0">Why Client-Side PDF Processing Matters</h3>
          <p class="mb-0 text-zinc-400">
            Most online PDF tools upload your files to their remote servers to process them. This is a massive privacy risk. SolversPro uses modern WebAssembly (Wasm) and JavaScript technologies to process PDFs directly on your device. Your data never leaves your computer, making our tools safe for enterprise and confidential use.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-6">Ready to streamline your workflow?</h2>
        <p>
          Stop paying for premium subscriptions for basic PDF tasks. Explore our entire <a href="/all-tools#section-tools">PDF Toolkit</a> today and experience lightning-fast, secure document manipulation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <BlogShare url="https://solverspro.com/blog/top-5-free-online-pdf-tools" title="Top 5 Free Online PDF Tools for Editing, Merging, and Protecting Documents" />
      <BlogRating />
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
